  "behavior": [
    "Admission uses only current approved session namespaces, with method and complete chain/account tuple from one grant; required/optional proposal namespaces do not grant authority.",
    "Captures acknowledged, unexpired session topic, peer key, canonical HTTP(S) peer origin, local session revision, available account and one eligible EVM catalog network/provider. Scam/INVALID verification and mismatched VALID origins fail closed.",
    "Copies the incoming payload before any network activation and copies context into the private UUID queue. Activation completion must still match the captured authorization.",
    "Approval revalidates the captured context before key access and after each asynchronous deny-list/provider/population boundary. Session updates, deletion, expiry and local disconnect invalidate earlier revisions, including changed-away-and-back sessions.",
    "Unsigned ethers VoidSigner population precedes key export. Detached Wallet signing is followed by a final context/provider check before broadcast; message and typed signatures are checked again before release.",
    "Provider chain is checked and the transaction chain is explicitly fixed to the captured network. Actual signed bytes and recovered legacy child signer are verified in tests.",
    "Transaction submission failures consume the intent as an ambiguous broadcast; failed pre-submission context checks remain rejectable without permitting stale-context signing. A local deny-list block consumes its rejected intent. Canonical peer origin supplies the popup requester input."
  ],
